> SCOPE RULED: (C) + For all four frontends on unlinked semantic/stack/register lanes, assert correct completed iteration and D(16)=D(64)=D(256); linked recursive depths at 8/32/128 remain a required characterization follow-up, with no growth lower-bound assertions.

sol has already confined the *constant-case contract* (the only thing ever ASSERTED) to **unlinked** lanes, and pushed the linked recursive characterization to a named follow-up. The full blocking-aware driver is not what sol's (C) requires for the assertion pillar.

**2. Round 1 BLOCKED (terra, linked)** — the linked depth experiment did not complete: linked composition requires scheduler / FFI-bridge / link-serving handling *during stepping*; the existing utility measures unlinked runs only. This is the linked-warm machinery, correctly deferred.

**3. Round 2 BLOCKED (terra, unlinked)** — the existing depth helper treats blocking as completion; it cannot distinguish a VM parked on a scheduler/FFI effect from a finished program.

**4. The decisive refinement (owner-surfaced, and it dissolves the Round 2 blocker):** the fixture set is *deliberately pure* — loops, try/finally, caught failures, **no FFI effects**. Pure guest code on unlinked semantic/stack/register lanes runs synchronously to completion: no effects fire, no parking happens, so there is no "parked-on-effect" state to misread as completion. The blocking-as-completion defect **cannot bite** on pure unlinked fixtures. A driver scoped to those fixtures needs only "step until the continuation is empty, track max-K" — no completion-vs-blocking state machine at all.

The full driver (option (a)) therefore builds machinery that is only exercised in the linked-warm follow-up, which sol's (C) already names and specifies separately. Building it now spends a strong-lane round on a driver whose assertion half doesn't use it.

**Why not (b):** the prime directive is "measured, never asserted," and depth is the *last* pillar — encoding/contract/provenance are already measured and merged. Descopping leaves the one pillar the mod's Q4 exists to pin as a documented hole. (a′) keeps the pillar measured *now* on the surface sol's (C) already authorizes.

**Why not (c):** sol's (C) is complete and correct; sol is the review lane. Re-routing breaks a reservation to no purpose.

